Tradespeople aren't the only businesses that benefit from a managed starter website. Any local service business that needs to be found online — without the budget or appetite for a complex custom site — is a natural fit.

## Who this suits

**Cleaners**: Domestic and commercial cleaning businesses rely heavily on local search. A properly structured website with pages targeting your service areas makes the difference between appearing in Google and being invisible.

**Gardeners and landscapers**: People search "gardener near me" or "garden clearance [town]" regularly. A site with the right pages in place captures that traffic.

**Childminders and tutors**: Parents searching for childcare or tuition in their area want to see a professional online presence before making contact. A website that clearly sets out what you offer and where you work builds trust before the first call.

**Dog walkers and pet sitters**: Local pet services are searched constantly. A clean website with your services, prices, and location sets you apart from the people still relying solely on Facebook groups.

**Mobile beauticians, therapists, and wellbeing practitioners**: Clients want to know what you offer, your availability, and how to book. A website handles all of that without requiring you to respond to every enquiry manually.

## What makes a managed starter website the right choice

For most local service businesses, the website's job is simple: appear in Google for relevant local searches, give a good first impression, and make it easy to get in touch. A managed starter website is built to do exactly that.

You don't need a bespoke design or a complex booking system. You need a professional site, a proper domain, and enough pages to rank for the services and locations you cover. That's what every plan delivers — and what the monthly page additions build on over time.

